>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">10.80<br/>July 21, 2015<br/>Summer Update 2015</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p>The <b>Vandura Wyrm Cave</b> is a cave east of <a href=\"#/wiki/Liberty%20Bay\">Liberty Bay</a>, very close to town, accessed <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"32388,32842,7\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">here (32388, 32842, 7)</a>. It is comparable to the <a href=\"#/wiki/Drefia%20Wyrm%20Lair\">Drefia Wyrm Lair</a>, but a lot quicker to access. There is space to run around, but also hills and passages to hunt the Wyrms one by one. \n</p><p>The ground floor only has normal <a href=\"#/wiki/Wyrm\">Wyrms</a>, but the hills also has <a href=\"#/wiki/Elder%20Wyrm\">Elder Wyrms</a>. The majority of them spawning in pairs.\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Creatures\">Creatures</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Ground_Floor\">Ground Floor</span></h3>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">HP</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Max. Damage</th><th style=\"font-size: small;\">Loot</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 100px; text-align: center\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" type